This directory is intentionally empty, and must stay that way.

It is the deployment's "output directory". Vercel checks the output directory
for a matching static file BEFORE it evaluates the `routes` in vercel.json, and
serves any hit straight from the CDN. Anything placed here is therefore served
without passing through Express — bypassing the /data and /landing-page guards,
the admin session check and the static allow-list.

Keeping it empty is what forces every request to reach the Express app, which is
where all of Antara's routing and access control actually lives.

Do not add files here. Public assets belong at the repository root (images/,
audio/, photos sites/, *.css, *.js) and are served by Express.
